## 5. Subprocess Integration Architecture Notice

The multimedia framework **FFmpeg** and speech synthesis engine **Piper** are integrated into DubbiOvi exclusively as isolated external binary processes.
- Execution occurs strictly via Node.js `child_process.spawn`.
- Communication is limited to command-line parameters, standard input/output streams, and temporary disk files.
- No static library linking, dynamic library loading (`dlopen`, `.dylib`, `.dll`, `.so`), shared memory IPC, or C/C++/Python language bindings are used.

This verified technical architecture — operating independent binary executables with process boundary isolation and no shared memory or static/dynamic code linking — supports treating FFmpeg and Piper as separate components whose GPL compliance is managed independently from DubbiOvi's own application codebase.
